  "text": " Exercise 147. Regular transitions of adjectives and verbs. A different change occurs when you go from an adjective or a noun to a verb. The stress stays in the same place, but the M-A-T in an adjective is completely reduced to met, whereas in a verb it's a full A sound, mate. Repeat. advocate to advocate animate to animate alternate to alternate appropriate to appropriate approximate to approximate articulate to articulate associate to associate deliberate to deliberate Discriminate to discriminate. Duplicate to duplicate. Elaborate to elaborate. An estimate to estimate. Graduate to graduate. Intimate to intimate. Moderate to moderate. Predicate to predicate. Separate. To separate,",
